' F8 -- The ingestion pipeline at the thesis revision (dfc20df6).
' HERO FIGURE. Chapter 4.
' Claim supported: two entry routes (the classic SSE stream and the v4 poll
' routes) admit a PDF synchronously and converge on one stored object and one
' Arq job; the job does all content work server-side and persists page by
' page, so the reader can open the file long before the parse finishes.
' Each page is routed once per parse (page text counted without running
' footers): < 25 chars -> no_text, vision, flagged for review; < 150 chars
' with figures covering >= 5% of the page -> figure, vision adds title and
' summary, the page keeps its own text; else text, batched 8 per call.
' Sources: upload.py:146-266 (SSE route), :571-763 (batch);
' v4_spaces.py:180-195 + materials_service.py:105-146 (v4 route);
' v4_spaces_service.py:477-536 (instant reader); unified_orchestrator.py:
' 842-885 (run row, guards), :898-1023 (extract, enhance), :919 (routes),
' :1054-1214 (pages; routes applied :1080), :1245-1285 (deck quiz), :1285-1438
' (finalize), :1441-1499 (failure path); page_blocks.py:201-219 (route_page).
' Not drawn, on purpose: the headroom gate (:927-940; cannot trip while an
' unmetered provider such as OpenAI is configured) and the flag-gated steps
' that are off in production (Studio pages, course context, cross-lecture
' quiz, review cards, concept graph). The reject label is padded with
' no-break spaces so PlantUML does not run it into the diamond.
' Size budget: <= 715 x 935 px at 80 dpi, so labels print at >= 6.5 pt.
@startuml f8-pipeline
!include _style.iuml
skinparam ConditionEndStyle hline

partition "API request (synchronous)" {
start
if (route) then (classic: SSE)
  :POST /upload/parse-pdf-stream
  read <= 50 MB, PDF <= 300 pages, sha256
  parse cache, student quota, queue < 50;
else (v4: poll)
  :POST /v4/uploads  or  /upload/batch
  read, validate, sha256, owner dedupe
  student quota (batch: queue < 50);
endif
if (admitted?) then (yes)
  :store pdf-uploads/<sha256>.pdf and enqueue:
  the v4 reader opens the original PDF now (polls every 3 s); <<output>>
  note right
    Pentagon (send signal):
    the reader gains something.
  end note
else ( no: 400 / 403 / 413 / 429, or duplicate  )
  stop
endif
}

partition "Arq worker (asynchronous, durable)" {
-> claim job, upsert parse_runs row;
if (run completed?) then (yes: replay from DB)
  stop
elseif (lock held?) then (yes: return early)
  stop
elseif (spend cap hit?) then (yes: run FAILED)
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Extract: PyMuPDF text per page, page count stored.
Enhance: title + summary (text layer only), create or
reuse the lecture row, poster, compacted reader copy.;
if (page route (set once per parse)?) then (text)
  :one LLM call per 8 pages;
else (no_text: < 25 chars\nfigure: < 150 chars, figures >= 5%)
  :vision per page; figure keeps its text, no_text flagged;
endif
:persist each page, start its embedding task; <<output>>
:Deck quiz: 5-8 questions, each citing its slide, re-answered
by a checker call without the key: dispute -> one repair, else drop.
Finalize: quiz, description, slide count, parse receipt, localise EN/DE,
join embeddings (<= 120 s, one retry), attach them, run COMPLETED.;
stop
}

note right
  Any exception or the 900 s timeout:
  partial lecture finalized, run FAILED,
  error event, lock released. No retry.
end note

@enduml
